course: dictionary
lesson: 10959
title: A wallet and what it holds
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A wallet is a small flat case for keeping money, cards and tickets. The words around it give clues: «Picture finding a wallet with forty pounds and an address card inside» shows what a wallet holds.
explain: «Keep your money in a zipped pocket or a wallet so it is harder to lose or steal» tells you a wallet keeps money safe. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: "keep your money in a small flat case so it is harder to lose" still makes sense.
explain: A digital wallet is different. It is an app on a phone that holds bank cards, so you can pay with your phone. The word wallet is used for both, so read the rest of the sentence to tell which one it means.
fact: A wallet is a small flat case, usually folded, for keeping money, cards and tickets.
fact: A digital wallet is an app on a phone that holds bank cards to pay with.
fact: «A found wallet or purse is given to a parent, a shop or the police without taking anything.»
fact: In a big 2019 study across 40 countries, more people returned lost wallets when there was more money inside.
fact: «Wallet-friendly» means cheap, so it does not cost much money.
exercise: «Dad put the bus ticket back in his wallet.» Where did Dad keep the ticket? | On the roof | *In his wallet | Under the bed | In the garden shed
exercise: Maya had £10 in her wallet and took out £4. How much money is left? | £40 | *£6 | £14 | £4
exercise: «Finding a wallet and handing it in is the honest thing to do.» What is the honest thing to do with a found wallet? | *Give it to a parent, a shop or the police | Keep the money | Spend the money inside it | Throw it away
test: «Picture finding a wallet with forty pounds and an address card inside.» What is a wallet used for here? | Growing plants | Playing a game | *Keeping money and cards | Cooking dinner
test: A digital wallet is an app on a phone. What does it hold? | Football boots | *Bank cards to pay with | Pets | Books and toys
exam: «In a big crowd, hold an adult's hand.» Which word in the sentence means a small flat case for money? | *wallet | hand | crowd | adult
